  "problem": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region bounded between the ellipses $(x-1)^{2}+4{y}^{2}=1$ and ${x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=4?$\n\n- It is a type I region\n- It is a type II region\n- It's neither a type I nor a type II region",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/215dd0c920e700a75896fc54751ec20d197487a2c992cd8910810c66129c14dc.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- The vertical line $x=1$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type I region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/7e1a0c5dd2b4aadf7efe78d903234b8d00cf4fa92eb7a3b41209a856f2d14b01.png)\n\n- The horizontal line $y=0.25$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type II region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14038811/assets/a90d7306e3f88a31609e368f9362248d6a12b7922b6a9e8c9f980ab31e7fb140.png)\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true.",
